# Service logs, hang diagnostics (.logs/hangs: stack samples, open-file lists, log tails) and pid / watchdog
# state written by start-local.sh and scripts/stack_watchdog.sh: host-specific runtime files (desktop review
# R-OPS-14). The Next dev build and node_modules are rebuilt by npm (once: git rm -r --cached ui/node_modules
# ui/.next, see docs/RUNBOOK_RESTORE.md 'Version control and off-machine backup').
.logs/
.pids/
ui/node_modules/
ui/.next/

# Desktop app (Tauri v2): Rust build output, the pinned CLI, generated ACL schemas
desktop/src-tauri/target/
desktop/node_modules/
desktop/src-tauri/gen/

# UI audit / QA screenshots: pages such as PORT and BRKR can show broker session details (desktop review C1-trader-ux-05)
reports/ui_audit/**/*.png
reports/desktop_app/**/*.png
reports/worldclass_program/**/*.png

# ── publishing hygiene (5 Nov 2026: the repo is pushed to a PUBLIC GitHub remote) ─────────────────────────────────
# runtime state, databases, snapshots, paper/live books, caches: never in git (restore recipe: docs/RUNBOOK_RESTORE.md)
data/
# logs of every service (they can carry request URLs and account details)
*.log
*.log.[0-9]*
logs/
services/*/logs/
# screenshots and scratch downloads in research reports (audit sets include account pages; regenerate with the harnesses)
reports/**/*.png
reports/**/*.jpg
reports/**/*.jpeg
reports/**/*.webp
reports/**/scratch/
reports/**/shots*/
# raw files too large for git (re-derivable by the report's own script)
reports/poc_conditional/strategy_trades.csv
# tool caches and assistant working memory
graphify-out/
.claude/agent-memory/
.remember/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
